\f0\b\fs32 \cf2 1. The Operator-Level Mismatch and the Collapse of Equivariance
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\tx680\li680\fi-480\slleading120\sa174\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs40 \cf2 \'95	
\f0\b\fs32 The Claim:
\f1\b0  The framework requires 
\f2\i equivariance
\f1\i0  during Stage 2: the dissipative lock must preserve the populations of the measured projector while scrambling its phase, carrying the prepared 
\fs24 \cf0 \uc0\u8237 $|\\cdot|^2$
\fs32 \cf2 \uc0\u8236  weights intact to the outcome.
\fs24 \cf0 \

\f3\fs40 \cf2 \'95	
\f0\b\fs32 The Failure:
\f1\b0  As admitted in \'a73.7, the electromagnetic interaction couples via the vector current (
\fs24 \cf0 \uc0\u8237 $\\bar\{\\psi\}\\gamma^\\mu\\psi$
\fs32 \cf2 \uc0\u8236 ), which is chirality-preserving. This transverse coupling acts as a driving force that induces relaxation toward the ground state of the system or causes dephasing, dynamically erasing the input weights. The only operator capable of acting as a non-demolition measurement on the 
\fs24 \cf0 \uc0\u8237 $\\bar\{\\psi\}\\psi$
\fs32 \cf2 \uc0\u8236  (scalar) channel is a scalar Yukawa or gravitational coupling. However, as noted in \'a74.4, the author correctly rejects macroscopic gravitational coherence rates (
\fs24 \cf0 \uc0\u8237 $\\sim GM^2/\\hbar\\Delta z$
\fs32 \cf2 \uc0\u8236 ) as dimensional artifacts.
\fs24 \cf0 \

\f3\fs40 \cf2 \'95	
\f0\b\fs32 The Consequence:
\f1\b0  If the EM interaction cannot preserve the weights of the chiral interference channel, and the gravitational channel is too weak to operate on quantum timescales (
\fs24 \cf0 \uc0\u8237 $\\sim 10^\{16\}$
\fs32 \cf2 \uc0\u8236 \'96
\fs24 \cf0 \uc0\u8237 $10^\{24\}$
\fs32 \cf2 \uc0\u8236  s), then the framework has no physical mechanism to enforce equivariance for the proposed chiral binary. The synchronization mechanism actively 
\f2\i destroys
\f1\i0  the state's memory before it can select a basin based on its prepared amplitudes.
\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\tx680\li680\fi-480\slleading120\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs40 \cf2 \'95	
\f0\b\fs32 Fix:
\f1\b0  The author must either: (a) identify an unsuppressed, physical, non-demolition EM coupling to a different bilinear that mirrors this behavior, or (b) explicitly concede that MCI cannot use the internal chiral 
\fs24 \cf0 \uc0\u8237 $L/R$
\fs32 \cf2 \uc0\u8236  phase as the universal measurement register, shifting the synchronization mechanics entirely to standard macroscopic pointer-state einselection.
\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\slleading120\sb340\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf2 2. The "Why Squared" Vacuum Measure Barrier
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\tx680\li680\fi-480\slleading120\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs40 \cf2 \'95	
\f0\b\fs32 The Claim:
\f1\b0  The Born rule is reframed as the measure of background configurations that select a given basin (\'a77.3), with relaxation to quantum equilibrium (
\fs24 \cf0 \uc0\u8237 $H$
\fs32 \cf2 \uc0\u8236 -theorem) suggested as the dynamical route (\'a78).
\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\tx680\li680\fi-480\slleading120\sa174\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs40 \cf2 \'95	
\f0\b\fs32 The Failure:
\f1\b0  In a synchronization model where a system is driven into a discrete set of attracting wells by an unbiased background field, the geometric basin volume of a symmetrically balanced Adler/Kuramoto model is fundamentally uniform (e.g., 50/50 for a binary split). To recover 
\fs24 \cf0 \uc0\u8237 $|\\alpha|^2$
\fs32 \cf2 \uc0\u8236 , the initial probability density of the background field itself must be precisely distributed according to a 
\fs24 \cf0 \uc0\u8237 $|\\psi|^2$
\fs32 \cf2 \uc0\u8236  weight. The invocation of Valentini\'92s sub-quantum 
\fs24 \cf0 \uc0\u8237 $H$
\fs32 \cf2 \uc0\u8236 -theorem is unsupported here: Valentini's derivation relies on non-local, non-lin
\f2\i ear guidance equat
\f1\i0 ions for particle positions in Bohmian mechanics. It has never been proven that a dissipative, boundary-localized phase-locking equation satisfies the necessary mixing and continuity properties to yield a 
\fs24 \cf0 \uc0\u8237 $|\\psi|^2$
\fs32 \cf2 \uc0\u8236  attractor in phase space.
\fs24 \cf0 \

\f3\fs40 \cf2 \'95	
\f0\b\fs32 Fix:
\f1\b0  Provide a concrete mathematical sketch of the sub-quantum distribution function for the background field, or explicitly state that the 
\fs24 \cf0 \uc0\u8237 $|\\psi|^2$
\fs32 \cf2 \uc0\u8236  weighting of the background ensemble is a fundamental, non-derived postulate of the theory, matching Bohm's quantum equilibrium hypothesis.
